had never before seen a rabbit with either a waistcoat pocket or a watch to

17
00:01:21,799 --> 00:01:26,658
take out of it, and burning with curiosity, she ran across the field after

18
00:01:26,659 --> 00:01:34,218
it unfortunately was just in time to see it pop down a large rabbit hole under the hedge.

19
00:01:34,219 --> 00:01:39,617
In another moment down went Alice after it, never once considering how in the

20
00:01:39,618 --> 00:01:42,077
world she was to get out again.

21
00:01:42,078 --> 00:01:46,878
The rabbit hole went straight on like a tunnel for some way, and then dipped

22
00:01:46,879 --> 00:01:51,859
suddenly down, so suddenly that Alice had not a moment to think about stopping

23
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:56,779
herself before she found herself falling down a very steep well.

24
00:01:56,780 --> 00:02:02,119
Either the well was very deep, or she fell very slowly, for she had plenty of

25
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:07,877
time as she went down to look about her and to wonder what was going to happen next.

26
00:02:07,878 --> 00:02:12,859
First, she tried to look down and make out what she was coming to, but it was

27
00:02:12,860 --> 00:02:16,877
too dark to see anything; then she looked at the sides of the well,

28
00:02:16,878 --> 00:02:21,859
and noticed that they were filled with cupboards and bookshelves here and there

29
00:02:21,860 --> 00:02:25,097
she saw maps and pictures hung upon pegs.

30
00:02:25,098 --> 00:02:30,018
She took down a jar from one of the shelves as she passed; it it was labeled

31
00:02:30,019 --> 00:02:34,817
ORANGE MARMALADE”, but to her great disappointment it was empty:

32
00:02:34,818 --> 00:02:39,859
she did not like to drop the jar for fear of killing somebody so managed to

33
00:02:39,860 --> 00:02:44,899
put it into one of the cupboards as she fell past it. “Well!” thought Alice to

34
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:48,799
